# The SQLite database and its WAL. Seeded from the repo's own artefacts with `npm run seed`,
# so it is always rebuildable and never belongs in git.
#
# ANCHORED, and it has to be: `data/` without the leading slash matches a directory called
# `data` at ANY depth, which silently swallowed `client/src/data/` — a source directory —
# the moment one was added. A file that git never offers to add is a file nobody notices is
# missing until the build fails on somebody else's machine.
/data/
# The backups tools/wipe-demo.js writes beside it, for the same reason.
/data/backup-*/
# Dev key material. The site's invite-signing private key is generated on first boot; it is a
# development key and must never be committed or reused in production.
keys/
node_modules/
client/node_modules/
client/dist/
